    "How ClipVault works" : {

    },
    "Image" : {

    },
    "iOS does not let any app watch the clipboard in the background, and ClipVault does not try to. It saves what you choose to save, plus, if you allow it, the clipboard when the app or keyboard opens." : {

    },
    "iOS never tells apps when you copy, so copies are saved only while ClipVault or its keyboard is open, and only the latest copy survives in between. Sharing to ClipVault also copies the shared item, so the next paste gives it. The keyboard needs Allow Full Access. iOS may ask permission to paste unless you set Paste from Other Apps to Allow in ClipVault's iOS settings." : {

    },
    "Items you save by tapping Paste, using the Share sheet, or running a Shortcut. If you leave these options on, it also saves the clipboard when the app opens and when the ClipVault keyboard is open (the keyboard needs Full Access). You can turn both off in Settings. ClipVault never watches your clipboard while it is closed or in the background." : {

    },
